       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At that level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose or frequency.**\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
